    scenario A: the Pass-1 sequence as a Vertex AI Workbench notebook that witnesses the SQL; runbook corrections
    
    notebooks/cloudbq_deploy_and_witness.ipynb mirrors the Cloud Shell runbook one cell per deploy.sh step (DRYRUN=1 all, check-env …
    invoker, dry as the gate, run SEALSQ, run ICALPS, probe), then executes the repo's SQL through the BigQuery client with the job
    id, statement type, bytes processed, slot time and cache flag printed next to each statement: INFORMATION_SCHEMA, the hot_score_v1
    UDF and the 15 golden vectors (ok = TRUE), main.hot_score on the same vectors side by side, report_state / new_deals_runs /
    new_deals_history / new_deals_last_7d, probe from the shell and from Python (equality check), the dry payload fetched with an ID
    token chosen by credential type, and an optional live parity check (HubSpot deals of the last 7 days through main.hot_score and
    the UDF via test_hot_score.emit_sql). `enable` follows the witness section behind a flag. The token is prompted (getpass) and
    passed as an environment variable only; .env is written from a SETTINGS dict without clobbering hand edits.
    
    Reviewed adversarially before commit (fixed: TIMESTAMP_MILLIS on a TIMESTAMP column, ID-token fallback unreachable on a VM,
    write-once settings cell, pull on a dirty tree, pip outside the kernel, NULL-skipping assert). Executed offline with a real
    kernel: every cell that needs no credentials runs; the rest stop at the credential boundary.
    
    Runbook (docs/PASS1_SEQUENCE.md): the operator role list now covers enable-apis, iam and the --source deploy; `.env` is sourced
    before the hand-typed look commands; the token is read with `read -rsp` instead of appearing in history; `$D url | tail -1`;
    the idempotency check uses `replay` (a second `run` opens the next window). notebooks/README.md explains the two credential
    stores on a Workbench instance. tests/test_notebook.py keeps the notebook valid, compilable, complete, flag-guarded and output-free;
    CI installs nbformat for it.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
